From: MiceWine <micewine@localhost>
Subject: winebrowser: Fix pointer types in Android socket calls

Mismo problema exacto que el patch 0005 (dlls/user32/clipboard.c), pero en el otro
lugar donde la rama proton-9.0-arm64ec de Pipetto habla por socket con el lado
Android: programs/winebrowser/main.c pasa int* directo a send(), cuyo prototipo
Winsock declara const char*.

GCC lo aceptaba con warning; clang lo trata como ERROR
(-Wincompatible-pointer-types), asi que con el toolchain PE cambiado a llvm-mingw
(necesario para arm64ec, ver --with-mingw en build.sh) el build muere en:

  ../programs/winebrowser/main.c:88:22: error: incompatible pointer types passing
      'int *' to parameter of type 'const char *'
  make: *** [Makefile:202367: programs/winebrowser/aarch64-windows/main.o] Error 1

Fix: casts explicitos a const char*, igual que en 0005. No cambia una sola
instruccion generada -- solo satisface el chequeo de tipos.

--- a/programs/winebrowser/main.c
+++ b/programs/winebrowser/main.c
@@ -85,12 +85,12 @@
 	}
 	int net_requestcode = htonl(message.request_code);
 	int net_data_length = htonl(strlen(message.data));
-	ret = send(sock_fd, &net_requestcode, sizeof(net_requestcode), 0);
+	ret = send(sock_fd, (const char *)&net_requestcode, sizeof(net_requestcode), 0);
 	if (ret == SOCKET_ERROR) {
 		TRACE( "Failed to send request code to server\n" );
 		return 0;
 	}
-	ret = send(sock_fd, &net_data_length, sizeof(net_data_length), 0);
+	ret = send(sock_fd, (const char *)&net_data_length, sizeof(net_data_length), 0);
 	if (ret == SOCKET_ERROR) {
 		TRACE( "Failed to send data length to server\n" );
 		return 0;
